# 7. Required First-Slice Prompt Capabilities

Support existing request payloads for these ordinary non-spatial interactions:

## Select One

Examples:

- casting slot/payment option
- damage type
- action mode

## Select Many

Examples:

- generic refinement list where a modal/list presentation is appropriate

Respect existing min/max/required semantics supplied by the request.

## Boolean / Optional Choice

Examples:

- use an optional enhancement
- decline an optional feature

Distinguish “decline optional choice” from “cancel required parent action.”

## Number

Validate min/max from the request.

## Resource Choice

Render legal payment/resource options already supplied by Configuration/Payment discovery. Do not
rediscover payment legality in UI.

## Damage Type

Render only the legal values already supplied by the configuration source. Never expose a universal
“all damage types” dropdown.

## Manual / Physical Roll Entry

Bridge manual/physical RollProvider input requirements through the existing `roll` pending request.
For D20 rolls, default to natural die entry when the RollRequest expects natural input; WildPath
applies known modifiers and preserves natural 1/20 semantics.

