# 18. Serialization and Mutation

Request/response data crossing ResolutionState must remain plain serializable data. Reject/isolate:

- Map
- Date
- arbitrary class instances
- Foundry Documents
- Applications
- DOM nodes
- functions/callbacks
- Promises

Do not use lossy JSON cloning to “make” invalid data serializable.

Prompt rendering, preview refresh, and response collection must not mutate Actors, Items, Effects,
resources, or Action Economy. Mutation remains behind the later transaction/commit boundary.

